1  # ADR-166: operator-facing CI messages naming a cause the job did not measure.
   # RATCHETS DOWN ONLY. Do not raise this to make a build pass -- a regression above it
   # means a new message asserts an unmeasured cause, which is the defect (#7242) that
   # blocked three production releases. Fix the message instead.
   #
   # The 1 is scripts/followthroughs/zot-soak-6122.sh, a PRE-EXISTING "Most likely cause"
   # in a soak probe, found the moment the scan was widened to scripts/. It is carried as a
   # ratcheting baseline rather than fixed here because it is an unrelated subsystem; that
   # is what a highwater is for. Everything this PR touches is at 0.
   #
   # THIS IS A CENSUS OF THE SCANNED SCOPE, NOT OF THE REPO. It counts only what DIRS walks
   # and only what OPERATOR_LINE + CLAIM detect; a known gap is tracked in #7318. "1" means
   # one detected offender in scope, never "one unmeasured causal claim exists anywhere".
   #
   # SCOPE WIDENING vs "RATCHETS DOWN ONLY". Those two rules meet on exactly one operation
   # and the file did not say which wins. They now do:
   #   - a CODE change may only LOWER this number. No exceptions; fix the message instead.
   #   - a SCOPE change (adding a DIRS entry) MAY set it to the newly measured value, and
   #     must record the widening + the measured delta as provenance in this comment.
   # Without that carve-out the next widening is unwritable — #7310 measured +0 so it never
   # hit the wall, but adding apps/web-platform/scripts/ takes the census 1 -> 3 (measured:
   # assert-dev-signin-eliminated.sh:104, run-migrations.sh:383) and would force the author
   # to either break the bold rule above or fix two messages in an unrelated subsystem as a
   # precondition of a scope change.
   #
   # DETECTION WIDENING, 2026-08-19 (#7578 + #7318) — AND WHY THIS NUMBER DID NOT MOVE.
   # Three changes to what the scanner can see:
   #   OPERATOR_LINE  + shell-variable assignment          (#7578)  measured +1
   #   OPERATOR_LINE  + continuation-line helper call      (#7318)  measured +1
   #   CLAIM          + static-prose dash appendix         (#7578)  measured +9
   #   MEASURED       appendix class now needs an explicit MEASURED-BY  measured +1
   # Census 1 -> 12 on the widening, then 12 -> 1 after all 11 newly-visible lines were
   # triaged. Every one was genuinely measured; none was an unmeasured causal claim.
   #
   # THE SCOPE CARVE-OUT ABOVE WAS AVAILABLE AND WAS DELIBERATELY NOT USED. Setting the
   # baseline to 12 was the obvious move and is what #7578 proposed. It was rejected for the
   # reason this file already gives about a two-hit broadening: a baseline carrying eleven
   # exonerated lines can never reach zero, and every future reader would read the 11 as real
   # offenders still outstanding. Annotation costs one comment per line and keeps the
   # invariant that makes this number worth reading — a non-zero count means a REAL offender.
   # So an unchanged `1` here does not mean nothing widened. It means the widening was paid
   # for at the call sites instead of in the baseline.
